body:
## Goal

Add automated **end-to-end tests for the role-based permission matrix** (PR #3) so the four role paths are checked on every PR instead of by hand. Each role signs in as a **real Firebase email/password test user** and we assert landing route, sidebar nav filtering, and route-guard redirects.

This was verified manually in a real browser for all four roles (localhost + the Cloudflare preview); this issue captures how to automate it.

## Current state

Scaffolding already landed in PR #3 and can be reused:

- `playwright.config.ts`
- `e2e/permissions.spec.ts`
- `e2e/helpers/auth.ts`
- `e2e/.test-credentials.example.json` (template; real file is gitignored)
- `e2e/README.md`
- `scripts/seed-test-user-docs.ts` (firebase-admin seeder)

The app now also has an **email/password sign-in form** (added in `a038cc6`), so tests can drive the real login UI — no test-only auth hook required.

## Roles under test

| Display name | Internal role | Test login env |
| ------------ | ------------- | -------------- |
| Full-timer   | `admin`       | `fulltimer`    |
| Trainee      | `manager`     | `trainee`      |
| Student      | `operator`    | `student`      |
| Community    | `viewer`      | `community`    |

Expected matrix (source of truth: `src/lib/permissions.ts`):

| Route | min role | viewer | operator | manager | admin |
|-------|----------|:------:|:--------:|:-------:|:-----:|
| `/` dashboard | operator | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| `/directory` | operator | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| `/board` stage | manager | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ |
| `/history` | manager | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ |
| `/admin/feedback` | admin | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ |
| `/attendance` `/prayer` `/settings` | viewer | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |

Viewer default route is `/attendance`; everyone else defaults to `/`.

---

## Prerequisites (one-time)

### 1. Test users exist in Firebase Auth (email/password) and have **approved `/users/{uid}` docs**
The app signs out any authenticated user without an approved user doc, so this is required. Two ways:

- **In-app invite (no service account):** sign in as an admin → Settings → Add Member → invite the four emails with roles Full-timer/Trainee/Student/Community. The approved `/users` doc is auto-created on each user's first sign-in.
- **Seed script (service account / ADC):**
  ```bash
  GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/sa.json npm run seed:e2e-users
  ```

### 2. Credentials file (gitignored)
```bash
cp e2e/.test-credentials.example.json e2e/.test-credentials.json
# fill in the real emails + passwords
```
Shape:
```json
{
  "fulltimer": { "email": "<email>", "password": "<pw>", "role": "admin",    "label": "Full-timer" },
  "trainee":   { "email": "<email>", "password": "<pw>", "role": "manager",  "label": "Trainee" },
  "student":   { "email": "<email>", "password": "<pw>", "role": "operator", "label": "Student" },
  "community": { "email": "<email>", "password": "<pw>", "role": "viewer",   "label": "Community" }
}
```

### 3. `VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY` available to the dev server / build
`firebase-applet-config.json` ships with a blank `apiKey`; the dev server reads `VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY` from `.env`. CI must provide it as a secret.

---

## Implementation plan

### `playwright.config.ts`
```ts
import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';

// Run against a deployed preview by setting E2E_BASE_URL; otherwise boot the dev server.
const baseURL = process.env.E2E_BASE_URL ?? 'http://localhost:3000';

export default defineConfig({
  testDir: './e2e',
  fullyParallel: true,
  workers: process.env.CI ? 2 : undefined,
  // Firebase Auth occasionally needs a retry on a cold page load; keep this small.
  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 1,
  reporter: process.env.CI ? [['github'], ['html', { open: 'never' }]] : 'list',
  use: {
    baseURL,
    trace: 'on-first-retry',
    // Tall enough that the sidebar footer (logout) is on-screen for 7-item roles (see #4).
    viewport: { width: 1280, height: 1000 },
  },
  projects: [{ name: 'chromium', use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] } }],
  webServer: process.env.E2E_BASE_URL
    ? undefined
    : { command: 'npm run dev', port: 3000, reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI, timeout: 60_000 },
});
```

### `e2e/helpers/auth.ts`
Drive the real email/password form. **Each Playwright test runs in its own isolated browser context**, so there is no shared Firebase auth state between roles — no logout step and none of the persistence races seen during manual testing.
```ts
import { type Page } from '@playwright/test';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';

const dir = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));
export type Role = 'fulltimer' | 'trainee' | 'student' | 'community';
interface Cred { email: string; password: string; role: string; label: string }

export function creds(): Record<Role, Cred> {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve(dir, '../.test-credentials.json'), 'utf8'));
  } catch {
    throw new Error('Missing e2e/.test-credentials.json — copy from .test-credentials.example.json');
  }
}

export async function signInAs(page: Page, role: Role) {
  const { email, password } = creds()[role];
  await page.goto('/');
  await page.getByPlaceholder('Email').waitFor({ state: 'visible' });
  // Let Firebase Auth finish initialising before submitting (prevents a cold-load race).
  await page.waitForTimeout(1500);
  await page.getByPlaceholder('Email').fill(email);
  await page.getByPlaceholder('Password').fill(password);
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: /sign in with email/i }).click();
  // The app shell (sidebar) only renders once authenticated AND approved.
  await page.getByLabel('Main Navigation').waitFor({ state: 'visible', timeout: 20_000 });
}
```

### `e2e/permissions.spec.ts`
```ts
import { test, expect, type Page } from '@playwright/test';
import { signInAs, type Role } from './helpers/auth';

const MATRIX: Record<Role, {
  landing: RegExp;
  navPresent: string[];
  navAbsent: string[];
  allowed: string[];
  denied: { from: string; to: RegExp }[];
}> = {
  community: {
    landing: /\/attendance$/,
    navPresent: ['Attendance', 'Prayer List', 'Settings'],
    navAbsent: ['Dashboard', 'Stage', 'Contacts', 'History'],
    allowed: ['/attendance', '/prayer', '/settings'],
    denied: [
      { from: '/', to: /\/attendance$/ },
      { from: '/board', to: /\/attendance$/ },
      { from: '/directory', to: /\/attendance$/ },
      { from: '/admin/feedback', to: /\/attendance$/ },
    ],
  },
  student: {
    landing: /\/$/,
    navPresent: ['Dashboard', 'Contacts', 'Attendance', 'Prayer List', 'Settings'],
    navAbsent: ['Stage', 'History'],
    allowed: ['/', '/directory', '/attendance', '/prayer', '/settings'],
    denied: [
      { from: '/board', to: /\/$/ },
      { from: '/history', to: /\/$/ },
      { from: '/admin/feedback', to: /\/$/ },
    ],
  },
  trainee: {
    landing: /\/$/,
    navPresent: ['Dashboard', 'Stage', 'Contacts', 'History', 'Attendance', 'Prayer List', 'Settings'],
    navAbsent: [],
    allowed: ['/', '/board', '/directory', '/history', '/attendance', '/prayer', '/settings'],
    denied: [{ from: '/admin/feedback', to: /\/$/ }],
  },
  fulltimer: {
    landing: /\/$/,
    navPresent: ['Dashboard', 'Stage', 'Contacts', 'History', 'Attendance', 'Prayer List', 'Settings'],
    navAbsent: [],
    allowed: ['/', '/board', '/directory', '/history', '/attendance', '/prayer', '/settings', '/admin/feedback'],
    denied: [],
  },
};

const navText = (page: Page) =>
  page.getByLabel('Main Navigation').getByRole('link').allInnerTexts().then(t => t.join(' '));

for (const role of Object.keys(MATRIX) as Role[]) {
  const m = MATRIX[role];
  test.describe(`role: ${role}`, () => {
    test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => { await signInAs(page, role); });

    test('lands on the correct default route', async ({ page }) => {
      await expect(page).toHaveURL(m.landing);
    });

    test('sidebar shows only permitted nav items', async ({ page }) => {
      const labels = await navText(page);
      for (const item of m.navPresent) expect(labels).toContain(item);
      for (const item of m.navAbsent) expect(labels).not.toContain(item);
    });

    test('allowed routes stay put', async ({ page }) => {
      for (const route of m.allowed) {
        await page.goto(route);
        await expect(page).toHaveURL(new RegExp(route.replace(/\//g, '\\/') + '$'));
      }
    });

    if (m.denied.length) {
      test('denied routes redirect to fallback', async ({ page }) => {
        for (const d of m.denied) {
          await page.goto(d.from);
          await expect(page).toHaveURL(d.to);
        }
      });
    }
  });
}
```

### `package.json`
```jsonc
"scripts": {
  "test:e2e": "playwright test",
  "seed:e2e-users": "tsx scripts/seed-test-user-docs.ts"
}
```

### Run it
```bash
# local dev server (auto-started by Playwright)
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=<key> npm run test:e2e

# against a deployed preview
E2E_BASE_URL=https://<preview>.pages.dev npm run test:e2e
```

---

## Why this avoids the manual-testing pitfalls

- **No logout / account-switch race.** Playwright gives each test a fresh, isolated browser context, so every role gets a clean Firebase auth state. The manual run shared one browser and had to log out between roles, which caused session-persist races and hit the clipped logout button (#4). Tests don't.
- **`displayName` provisioning bug is already fixed** (`a038cc6`): email/password accounts have a `null` displayName, which the Firestore rules reject on first-login `setDoc`. Without that fix, first-login provisioning fails with *"Missing or insufficient permissions"* and the app hangs on the loading skeleton.
- **Cold-load race** mitigated by the short settle in `signInAs` plus 1–2 Playwright retries.
- **Footer/logout viewport issue (#4)** avoided by a 1000px-tall viewport (and tests never click logout anyway).

## CI integration

```yaml
# .github/workflows/e2e.yml (sketch)
name: E2E permissions
on: [pull_request]
jobs:
  e2e:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with: { node-version: 20, cache: npm }
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npx playwright install --with-deps chromium
      - name: Write test credentials
        run: echo "$E2E_TEST_CREDENTIALS" > e2e/.test-credentials.json
        env: { E2E_TEST_CREDENTIALS: ${{ secrets.E2E_TEST_CREDENTIALS }} }
      - run: npm run test:e2e
        env: { VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY }} }
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        if: failure()
        with: { name: playwright-report, path: playwright-report/, retention-days: 7 }
```

Secrets required:
- `VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY` — Firebase web API key
- `E2E_TEST_CREDENTIALS` — the JSON contents of `e2e/.test-credentials.json`

Notes:
- These tests hit the **real** Firebase project. Keep them **read-only** (navigation/redirect assertions only — no data mutation) and consider gating on a label or running against the preview URL rather than on every push.
- Make the check **non-blocking** until it's proven stable, then add it to the branch ruleset.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] `npm run test:e2e` green locally against the dev server for all four roles
- [ ] Same green against a deployed preview via `E2E_BASE_URL`
- [ ] CI workflow runs on PRs with credentials from secrets
- [ ] `.test-credentials.json` and `playwright-report/` are gitignored (already are)
- [ ] README documents provisioning + how to run

Related: #4 (logout/account-switching UX), PR #3 (the permission feature being tested).
